course: dictionary
lesson: 791
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The word bee can name a flying insect, or it can mean a meeting or contest. To know which meaning is meant, read the words around it, which is its context.
explain: «The bee buzzed from flower to flower in the garden.» The clues are buzzed and flower, so this bee is an insect. «The class held a spelling bee on Friday.» The clues are spelling and class, so a bee is a contest where people try to spell words correctly.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in the meaning. Could a contest fit into the garden sentence? No. Could an insect fit into the spelling sentence? No. The meaning that still makes sense is the right one.
fact: A bee is a flying insect with a hairy body, often yellow and black striped.
fact: Bees collect nectar and pollen from flowers, and some bees make honey and wax.
fact: Bees are important pollinators: they carry pollen between flowers so plants can make fruit and seeds.
fact: A bee is also a meeting or contest, like a spelling bee.
fact: «Busy as a bee» means very busy, and «make a beeline» means go straight to a place.
exercise: «The bee buzzed from flower to flower in the garden.» What is the bee in this sentence? | A meeting where people vote | *A flying insect | A kind of flower | A spelling contest
exercise: «The class held a spelling bee on Friday.» What does bee mean here? | A flying insect with stripes | A bird that lays eggs | *A meeting or contest | A type of honey
exercise: Which sentence uses bee to mean a contest? | «A bee stung my arm at the park.» | «The bees made honey in the hive.» | «Bees have six legs.» | *«Ella won the spelling bee after three rounds.»
test: «Bees carry pollen between flowers so plants can make seeds.» What job do the bees do here? | *Carry pollen so plants can make seeds | Build hives out of wood | Sing to the flowers at night | Sell honey at the shop
test: «Longer, unmown grass lets clover and daisies bloom and feed bees and butterflies.» Which meaning of bee fits? | A meeting | A kind of flower | *A flying insect | A spelling contest
exam: Ella says «She made a beeline for the door» means she walked slowly around the room. What does it really mean? | *She went straight to the door | She stopped and waited by the wall | She walked slowly, looking at everything | She ran away from the door
